---
const routes = [
  { status: 'Working now', title: 'Android app and notifications', body: 'A person can choose an alert area, read attributable updates and decide whether notifications are useful to them.', tone: 'now' },
  { status: 'Pilot next', title: 'SMS for relevant notices', body: 'A bounded pilot could test concise, state-relevant delivery for people with limited data or no smartphone.', tone: 'next' },
  { status: 'Pilot next', title: 'USSD for essential access', body: 'Feature-phone access needs community, telecom and public-health partners before it can be offered responsibly.', tone: 'next' },
];
---

<section class="delivery-story" aria-labelledby="delivery-story-title" data-delivery-story>
  <div class="delivery-story__signal" data-story-reveal>
    <span class="eyebrow">The signal</span>
    <h3 id="delivery-story-title">A source stays attached to the message.</h3>
    <p>Every route starts with the same discipline: distinguish an official update from a modelled outlook, name the place it applies to, and show what the information cannot confirm.</p>
    <span class="delivery-story__boundary">No diagnosis · No fabricated reach data · No silent data sharing</span>
  </div>

  <div class="delivery-story__routes" aria-label="Current and future delivery routes">
    {routes.map((route, index) => (
      <article class:list={['delivery-route', `delivery-route--${route.tone}`]} data-story-reveal>
        <div class="delivery-route__line" aria-hidden="true"><i>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</i></div>
        <span>{route.status}</span>
        <h4>{route.title}</h4>
        <p>{route.body}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="delivery-story__footer" data-story-reveal>
    <p><strong>What is missing is as important as what is shown:</strong> SMS and USSD are not live services today. They need a scoped, approved pilot and accountable delivery partners.</p>
    <a class="button button--light" href="#inquiry" data-inquiry-topic="pilot">Explore a delivery pilot</a>
  </div>
</section>
